{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>I have divined, and YHWH has blessed me on your account</b> — for your sake and by your merit, for you are a righteous man. The meaning of נִחַשְׁתִּי is: I tested, and every נַחַשׁ is a נִסָּיוֹן (testing). And some say (Ibn Ezra) that he used to divine by means of teraphim. And Jacob said, <b>YHWH has blessed you at my foot</b> (Genesis 30:30); he did not wish to say \"on my account,\" out of humility, but said \"at my foot,\" because from the time my foot entered your house, you were blessed:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:43.047634096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}